Sharpen: on the last row the "next row" pointer was never set.

`if( y == y_max ) p_row = row;` assigns p_row where n_row was meant, so the
last row reads an uninitialised n_row: undefined behaviour; with OpenMP the
last row's result changes with the thread count (measured: exactly one row
differs between 1 and 8 threads). Clamp n_row to the row itself, mirroring
the first row's p_row.

--- a/src/processing/raw_processing.c
+++ b/src/processing/raw_processing.c
@@ -611,1 +611,1 @@
-            if( y == y_max ) p_row = row;    /* minimize border artifact */
+            if( y == y_max ) n_row = row;    /* minimize border artifact */
